diff --git a/source/medication-definition-module.html b/source/medication-definition-module.html
index 3aa518bc5e5..6c8792c5925 100644
--- a/source/medication-definition-module.html
+++ b/source/medication-definition-module.html
@@ -250,7 +250,7 @@ This module is concerned with resources and functionality in areas such as:
 	<p>There are other resources that are of particular interest to the medication definition domain.</p>
 	<ul>
 		<li> <a href="medication.html">Medication</a> This is the resource to use for prescribing use cases, and anywhere that an actual medication instance is needed.</li>
-		<li> <a href="substance.html">Substance</a> The substance resource has a limited subset of data, and is aimed at prescribing use cases. Unlike SubstanceDefinition, it can be an actual instance of a substance (e.g., an amount of an ingredient or raw material).</li>
+		<li> <a href="substance.html">Substance</a> The substance resource has a limited subset of data, and is aimed at prescribing use cases. Unlike SubstanceDefinition, it represents an actual instance of a substance (e.g., an amount of an ingredient or raw material).</li>
 		<li> <a href="devicedefinition.html">DeviceDefinition</a> A DeviceDefinition can be used to represent a device that is inside the package of a medicinal product, within the PackagedProductDefinition resource.</li>
 		<li> <a href="organization.html">Organization</a> Many regulatory processes are centred around organizations (pharma companies, drug manufacturers, regulatory agencies). These are all represented by Organizations, and are referenced by many of the module's resources.</li>
 	</ul>
